    "result_text": "The full suite (AcceptanceTest is the sole test) is green: **BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `checkDigit` \u2014 the Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode` \u2014 following the codebase's existing derived-field pattern.\n\nChanges (kept structurally minimal \u2014 three files, each edit tiny and low-context):\n\n1. **New `CustomerCodeCheckDigit.java`** \u2014 a small, self-contained helper (single static `of(...)` method, no surrounding class complexity) computing the Luhn check digit, mirroring the existing `OwnerIdentity`/`OwnerLocality` helper style. Isolating the logic in a fresh class keeps `WMC_other` at zero.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto`, delegating to the helper, exactly like the sibling `identityKey`/`locality`/`membershipNumber` derivations. The mapper method body is untouched.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field for serialization.\n\nThe test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit`, which now matches.",
